;
THE SYSOP'S CONSOLE

A - Local BYE controls
B - Between calls
C - Answering a chat page
:A
LOCAL BYE CONTROLS

During a call, the local keyboard can affect the caller's work.

Ctrl-B   Blank or unblank the caller
Ctrl-G   Toggle paging availability
Ctrl-Q   Enter sysop message mode
Ctrl-X   Leave sysop message mode
Ctrl-N   Force caller disconnect

While blanked, most control keys pass to the local application.
Keep the caller blanked during private work. Leave private programs
and return to A0: before unblanking. If using tmux, Ctrl-B Ctrl-B
passes a literal Ctrl-B to the guest.
:B
BETWEEN CALLS

At BYE's waiting prompt, local Ctrl-C opens its menu.
Select J to enter CP/M with BYE still attached. This is the
environment needed by AUTH. RETURN instead enters ordinary CP/M
without the resident BYE interface.
:C
ANSWERING A CHAT PAGE

A caller enters CHAT from CP/M. Answer with Escape on the local
keyboard. The upper pane is yours; the lower pane is the caller's.
Both ends need an 80x24 ANSI/VT100 terminal for split-screen CHAT.
CHAT /S is the plain scrolling alternative.

Ctrl-R redraws the split display. Ctrl-C or Ctrl-X ends chat.
Local Ctrl-B ends split chat and enters private operation.
